{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Lattice","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.bondRuleOfTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.bondRuleOfTower","kind":"def","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L247-L262","doc":"**A Markov tower with parameter `markovZ q` satisfies the bond rule.**\n\nGiven as a `def` rather than an `instance`: it is a construction to be applied\nto a specific tower, not something typeclass search should attempt to build. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.trivialMarkovTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.trivialMarkovTower","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L213-L229","doc":"The axioms are consistent and admit a **non-degenerate** model: `A = R`,\nevery `H n = ⊤`, every `σ n = 1`, `tr = id`, `z = 1`.\n\nPresent so `MarkovTower` is demonstrably not an empty abstraction. It is a\nwitness of inhabitation only — this model is commutative and says nothing about\nthe Hecke tower. Unlike a zero-functional witness it is at least faithful\n(`tr 1 = 1 ≠ 0` in a nontrivial `R`), so the axioms do not force degeneracy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.tr_wordProd_mul_bond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.tr_wordProd_mul_bond","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L197-L211","doc":"**The `(z + d)` bond rule**, now unconditional for monotone words.\n\nCombining the derived `σ_g` case with the linearity reduction of\n`QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear`: each bond letter `σ_g + d • 1` at an unused\ngenerator contributes exactly `z + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.tr_wordProd_mul_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.tr_wordProd_mul_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L130-L195","doc":"**The bond rule at an unused generator.**\n\nFor a monotone word `l` (strictly increasing letters) that does not use `g`,\n\n  `tr (wordProd l * σ g) = z * tr (wordProd l)`.\n\nThis is the single equation `qou-g8i1` left open, and it is derived here from\nthe Markov axioms — no extra hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.wordProd_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.wordProd_mem","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L117-L128","doc":"A word all of whose letters are below `n` lies in `H n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.wordProd_append_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.wordProd_append_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L113-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.wordProd_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.wordProd_nil","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.wordProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.wordProd","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L108-L109","doc":"The product of the generators listed by `l`, in order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.markov","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L104-L104","doc":"**The Markov property**, at the top of the tower only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.z","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.tr_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.tr_comm","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The trace property `tr (a * b) = tr (b * a)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.tr","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The trace, as a linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.far_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.far_comm","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L96-L96","doc":"Generators at distance `≥ 2` commute (the far-commutation braid relation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.σ_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.σ_mem","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L94-L94","doc":"`σ n` is the new generator at level `n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.σ","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L92-L92","doc":"The generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.H_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.H_mono","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The tower is increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.H","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The tower of subalgebras. `H n` is generated by `σ 0, …, σ (n-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator.MarkovTower","kind":"structure","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovUnusedGenerator.lean#L79-L104","doc":"A **Markov-trace tower**: the axioms of the Jones/Ocneanu trace on\n`H_1 ⊆ H_2 ⊆ ⋯`, with an abstract Markov parameter `z`.\n\nDeliberately minimal — every field below is used by the theorem, and no field\nencodes the conclusion. In particular there is no hypothesis about interior\ngenerators; that is what gets derived. ","signatureChunk":0}]}